{"name":"Lido Deck","hex":"#019294","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lido","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Part of the sea by a beach sectioned off for swimming and other aquatic activities.","An outdoor swimming pool."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Clipping of lidocaine"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lido"},{"term":"deck","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any raised flat surface that can be walked on: a balcony; a porch; a raised patio; a flat rooftop.","The floorlike covering of the horizontal sections, or compartments, of a ship or boat. Small vessels have only one deck; larger ships have two or three decks."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To furnish with a deck.","To knock (someone) to the floor, especially with a single punch."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deck"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lido (swimming pool)","blocks":[{"text":"In British English, a lido is a public outdoor swimming pool and surrounding facilities, or part of a beach where people can swim, lie in the sun, or participate in water sports. On a cruise ship or ocean liner, the lido deck features outdoor pools and related facilities."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Saltdean_Lido_-_geograph.org.uk_-_634728.jpg/330px-Saltdean_Lido_-_geograph.org.uk_-_634728.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lido_(swimming_pool)","wikidata":"Q1757063"},{"title":"Deck (ship)","blocks":[{"text":"A deck is a permanent covering over a compartment or a hull of a ship. On a boat or ship, the primary or upper deck is the horizontal structure that forms the \"roof\" of the hull, strengthening it and serving as the primary working surface. Vessels often have more than one level both within the hull and in the superstructure above the primary deck, similar to the floors of a multi-storey building, that are also referred to as 